{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 23 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D11"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the carboplatin shortage on 2023-04-28 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E32", "E22"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Accord Healthcare product on the shortage list is manufactured by Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited, which received an OAI classification letter dated 2023-04-05, 23 days before the posting.",
      "cites": ["E21", "D11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The OAI inspection ended 2022-12-02 and cited 11 observations including absence of written procedures and sterile drug product controls.",
      "cites": ["D7", "E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An import alert for Intas was published 2023-06-01 and a Warning Letter issued 2023-07-28, both after the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D8", "D9", "E19", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale East and Corvale Lakeside sites both use Teva Parenteral Medicines product labeled from PHARMACHEMIE BV, which is not the OAI plant.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E6", "E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 15.1 days of the 60 mL presentation and can spare 3 vials while keeping two weeks; Corvale Lakeside has 1.5 days and would reach 4 days after transfer.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3", "D13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked best option is to transfer 3 vials of 10 mg/mL, 60 mL from Corvale East to Corvale Lakeside.",
      "cites": ["D13"]
    }
  ]
}
